## Summary

ROUNDDOWN and TRUNC return #NUM! when asked to round the nonzero numbers 1234, -1234 or 0.5 toward zero at precision -309 or -400. The documented direction and precision semantics require zero for these inputs. The same functions return zero at precision -308, and zero input succeeds at all three tested precisions.

## Steps to reproduce

Use the source baseline under Runtime or environment. Save this small integration test as crates/functions/tests/rounding_boundary.rs. The calls and results below were executed through the public function API in a focused package test.

```rust
